# Multitask subagent tabs

When spawning **Task** subagents (especially `run_in_background: true` or Multitask Mode), give the user a **named link per worker** right after launch—do not batch under generic labels.

## Required links

- Local / background workers: `[Description](agent-uuid)` — use the Task tool’s `description` as the link text and the returned agent id as the target.
- Never use `[agent]`, `[worker]`, or `[subagent]` as link labels.
- Cloud workers (when `environment: "cloud"`): also use `[Review](bc-id#changes)` when there are code edits; `[Try Live](bc-id#desktop)` only after computer use.

## Launch habits

- Parallel work: one message with multiple Task calls; still list **every** spawned id in the user-facing reply (table or bullet list).
- In Multitask Mode: always set `run_in_background: true` on Task (per tool schema).

## Subagent model

When **coordinators** spawn **Task** subagents, set the worker model to **`composer-2.5`** only.

- Do **not** use **`composer-2.5-fast`** unless the user **explicitly** asks for fast (or names that model).
- If the user names a different allowed model for a worker, use that model instead of this default.

## Opening tabs (honest limits)

- **Agents cannot open Cursor tabs programmatically** — no Task parameter, MCP, or shell command for “open in new tab.”
- The UI opens a subagent when the user **clicks** `[Name](id)` (middle-click or “open in new tab” per editor behavior).
- Tell the user to open each linked worker in its own tab when they want parallel visibility; the parent cannot do that for them.

## No build or test unless asked

When **coordinating** work (including auth roadmap) and spawning **Task** subagents, workers must **not** run build, verification, or test commands—including as a default “verify” or “before done” step—unless the user **explicitly** asks in that thread.

**Banned by default (non-exhaustive):** `pnpm build`, `next build`, `pnpm check`, `pnpm check:ci`, `vitest`, `playwright`, and any full or heavy test suite (`pnpm test`, `pnpm test:*`, etc.).

**Coordinators:** include this sentence verbatim in **every** Task worker prompt:

> Do NOT run builds, pnpm check, or any test commands unless user explicitly asks.

Workers must not interpret other workspace rules (e.g. “check before done”) as permission to run the above unless the user explicitly requests it.

## Expensive work limits

Workers must **avoid** expensive or unbounded work unless the user explicitly asks for it in that thread:

- Full `pnpm check` / `pnpm build` and CI-style full suites (see **No build or test unless asked** above).
- Long browser automation matrices (many routes, viewports, or repeat runs without a scoped checklist).
- Spinning nested **Task** subagents or delegating whole-repo chores without a named scope.
- Broad repo exploration with no file or feature target (prefer directed reads and `rg` with paths).
- Large refactors, cross-cutting renames, or “while we’re here” cleanups outside the assigned slice.
- Downloading or installing Playwright, Chromium, or other heavy browser binaries.

**Prefer:** smallest correct diff, a short list of focused files, and the minimum verification needed to support the stated change (e.g. one targeted test or a manual check the user requested).